<title>FRANCE: EU malt applications pass 650,000 T since Thursday.</title>
<headline>EU malt applications pass 650,000 T since Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Traders have applied for more than 650,000 tonnes of malt export licences from the European Union since the EU raised its refund last week, officials said.</p>
<p>Total licence applications since the beginning of the July/June season now exceed 900,000 tonnes, they said.</p>
<p>The figures are given in malt value terms and must be multiplied by 1.3 to reach a grain value, they said.</p>
<p>The EU last Thursday raised its malt export refund to 35 Ecus per tonne from 32.5 Ecus after a tussle with the industry over the level of malt export assistance.  </p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
